# A generic function that builds a 'list of T' must banish it on return.
weave count_items shard T where T: Par with xs as list of T into int:
    var copy as list of T is list of T
    var i as int is 0
    while i < calling xs.len:
        calling copy.push with (xs at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return calling copy.len

weave main into int:
    var words as list of string is ["one", "two", "three"]
    var nums as list of int is [1, 2]
    var a as int is calling count_items with words
    var b as int is calling count_items with nums
    if a == 3 and b == 2:
        return 0
    return 1
